    {
      "entry": 17377,
      "name": "Keli'dan the Breaker",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:17377:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:25175d2cddddb54ff9bc8f4f",
            "source:bf756c027a3f06acc578cb90",
            "source:60075e97df2522519d4796d9",
            "source:dd1179fb3c76979a91cdd205",
            "source:fc67151e6d6af6611e79405d",
            "source:1dd8133ec4fb2374b474faa5"
          ],
          "text": "When interrupted, Keli'dan is alarmed that something has gone wrong and warns that “he” must not be let loose, fearing he will kill everyone. He blames the intruders, calls them ignorant, and threatens that their friends will soon join them. His words suggest he was trying to contain a danger, though they never identify who “he” is.",
          "when": {
            "entry": 17377
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": null
    },
